 zZIN1c5NFMzVkZKTkxJVDZMMy4u" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Cl
 ick Here</a>\n\n<i>NOTE: Registration closes 24 hours before event start.
  Please register ahead of the event. Registrants will receive Zoom inform
 ation and related materials by email one week and within 24 hours before 
 the event.</i>\n\nJoin an interactive event organized by ASIST. Reserve y
 our seat at the Research Integrity Roundtable "Open Scholarship: Data Tra
 nsparency\, Accessibility\, and Security" on Friday\, July 31st\, 2026 at
  12:00pm - 1:30pm EDT. This RCR-200 offering is designed for researchers 
 at every stage of their career\, regardless of their discipline. Particip
 ants will engage in an interactive virtual event to discuss the open scho
 larship framework and how you can make your data accessible\, transparent
 \, and secure.\n\nThis event is only open to current Duke faculty\, staff
 \, and students. Attending this event fulfills the <b>RCR-200</b> require
 ment for Faculty and Staff as well as the <b>714 RCR credit</b> for gradu
 ate students\, but participants must attend for 60 minutes and participat
 e in breakout room discussion to receive credit. \n\nContact: \nASIST off
 ice \nASIST@duke.edu
DURATION:PT1H30M
